4	Subject: [PATCH] Add simple versioning to the *-bridge-to-server protocol
5	
6	- In general, it is expected that clickhouse-*-bridges and
7	  clickhouse-server were build from the same source version (e.g. are
8	  upgraded "atomically"). If that is not the case, we should at least
9	  be able to detect the mismatch and abort.
10	
11	- This commit adds a URL parameter "version", defined in a header shared
12	  by the server and bridges. The bridge returns an error in case of
13	  mismatch.
14	
15	- The version is *not* send and checked for "ping" requests (used for
16	  handshake), only for regular requests send after handshake. This is
17	  because the internally thrown server-side exception due to HTTP
18	  failure does not propagate the exact HTTP error (it only stores the
19	  error as text), and as a result, the server-side handshake code
20	  simply retries in case of error with exponential backoff and finally
21	  fails with a "timeout error". This is reasonable as pings typically
22	  fail due to time out. However, without a rework of HTTP exceptions,
23	  version mismatch during ping would also appear as "timeout" which is
24	  too misleading. The behavior may be changed later if needed.
25	
26	- Note that introducing a version parameter does not represent a
27	  protocol upgrade itself. Bridges older than the server will simply
28	  ignore the field. Only servers older than the bridges receive an error
29	  but such a situation should never occur in practice.
